    "details": "Dinu Gherman reports:\n\n> The 2.3.1 fix for GHSA-555j-qj3j-c8jv stops \\\"renderUse()\\\" after\n> \\\"MAX_USE_EXPANSIONS\\\" (10,000) expansions. But each expansion\n> deep-copies and renders the whole referenced subtree, so the total\n> work is 10,000 \u00d7 (subtree size), and the subtree size is unbounded.\n> Nested \\<use\\> groups whose leaf group holds N rects make about 9,000\n> of the allowed expansions clone that leaf. In svglib 2.3.2, a\n> 2,254-byte SVG takes 68 s, and a 6,454-byte one (200 rects) takes 247\n> s and 2.6 GB RSS. The cost grows linearly with N. Only the SVG needs\n> to be attacker-controlled, as in GHSA-555j. main (6e79811) behaves the\n> same (50 rects: 62 s / 727 MB).\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0608",
